.TH "vsearch-userfields" "7" "April 29, 2026" "version 2.31.0" "vsearch manual"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
userfields \[em] output fields available with the --userout option
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The option \f[V]--userfields\f[R] selects and orders the columns written
to a \f[V]--userout\f[R] file.
Fields are separated by \f[V]+\f[R]:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
vsearch \[rs]
    --usearch_global queries.fasta \[rs]
    --db db.fasta \[rs]
    --id 0.97 \[rs]
    --userout results.tsv \[rs]
    --userfields query+target+id+alnlen+mism+opens
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
When a query has no match (reported only with
\f[V]--output_no_hits\f[R]), numeric fields are set to 0, string fields
are empty, and \f[V]target\f[R] is set to \f[V]*\f[R], unless noted
otherwise.
.PP
Fields are grouped thematically below.
See also \f[V]vsearch-pairwise_alignment_parameters(7)\f[R] for a
description of the alignment model and identity definitions.
.SS Alignment representation
.TP
\f[V]aln\f[R]
Pairwise alignment encoded as a string of operation characters:
\f[V]M\f[R] (match or mismatch, i.e.\ not a gap), \f[V]D\f[R] (deletion,
i.e.\ a gap in the target), \f[V]I\f[R] (insertion, i.e.\ a gap in the
query).
Empty if there is no alignment.
See \f[V]vsearch-cigar(5)\f[R] for a description of the operation
alphabet.
.TP
\f[V]caln\f[R]
Compact pairwise alignment in CIGAR format (Compact Idiosyncratic Gapped
Alignment Report): \f[V]M\f[R] (match or mismatch), \f[V]D\f[R]
(deletion, a gap in the target), \f[V]I\f[R] (insertion, a gap in the
query).
Explicit operations are always written (the \f[V]=\f[R] exact-match
shorthand appears only in \f[V]--uc\f[R] output).
Empty if there is no alignment.
See \f[V]vsearch-cigar(5)\f[R] for a complete description.
.TP
\f[V]qrow\f[R]
Query segment as seen in the pairwise alignment, with gap characters
inserted where the target has an insertion.
Empty if there is no alignment.
.TP
\f[V]trow\f[R]
Target segment as seen in the pairwise alignment, with gap characters
inserted where the query has an insertion.
Empty if there is no alignment.
.SS Query and target identifiers
.TP
\f[V]query\f[R]
Query sequence label.
.TP
\f[V]target\f[R]
Target sequence label.
Set to \f[V]*\f[R] if there is no alignment.
.SS Sequence lengths
.TP
\f[V]ql\f[R]
Query sequence length (positive integer).
.TP
\f[V]tl\f[R]
Target sequence length (positive integer).
.TP
\f[V]qs\f[R]
Query segment length.
Always equal to the query sequence length.
.TP
\f[V]ts\f[R]
Target segment length.
Always equal to the target sequence length.
.SS Alignment span
.PP
The following fields report the first and last aligned positions in the
query (q) or target (t) sequence, using 1-based nucleotide positions.
The \f[V]lo\f[R]/\f[V]hi\f[R] variants span the whole sequence, from 1
to its length (swapped for the query on minus-strand hits); the
\f[V]ilo\f[R]/\f[V]ihi\f[R] variants exclude terminal gaps and report
the span of the actual aligned residues.
.TP
\f[V]qlo\f[R]
First nucleotide of the query aligned with the target: 1 when there is
an alignment on the plus strand; on minus-strand hits \f[V]qlo\f[R] and
\f[V]qhi\f[R] are swapped (\f[V]qlo\f[R] is then the query sequence
length).
See \f[V]qilo\f[R] to exclude initial gaps.
.TP
\f[V]qhi\f[R]
Last nucleotide of the query aligned with the target: the \f[I]query
sequence length\f[R] when there is an alignment on the plus strand (1 on
minus-strand hits).
See \f[V]qihi\f[R] to exclude terminal gaps.
.TP
\f[V]qilo\f[R]
First nucleotide of the query aligned with the target, ignoring initial
terminal gaps.
Nucleotide positions use 1-based indexing.
.TP
\f[V]qihi\f[R]
Last nucleotide of the query aligned with the target, ignoring terminal
gaps at the right.
Nucleotide positions use 1-based indexing.
.TP
\f[V]tlo\f[R]
First nucleotide of the target aligned with the query.
Always 1 when there is an alignment (including terminal gaps at the
left).
See \f[V]tilo\f[R] to exclude initial gaps.
.TP
\f[V]thi\f[R]
Last nucleotide of the target aligned with the query: the \f[I]target
sequence length\f[R] when there is an alignment.
See \f[V]tihi\f[R] to exclude terminal gaps.
.TP
\f[V]tilo\f[R]
First nucleotide of the target aligned with the query, ignoring initial
terminal gaps.
Nucleotide positions use 1-based indexing.
.TP
\f[V]tihi\f[R]
Last nucleotide of the target aligned with the query, ignoring terminal
gaps at the right.
Nucleotide positions use 1-based indexing.
.SS Alignment statistics
.TP
\f[V]alnlen\f[R]
Length of the pairwise alignment: the number of columns, excluding
terminal gaps.
.TP
\f[V]ids\f[R]
Number of matching columns in the alignment (zero or positive integer).
.TP
\f[V]mism\f[R]
Number of mismatching columns in the alignment (zero or positive
integer).
.TP
\f[V]gaps\f[R]
Number of gap-containing columns in the alignment (zero or positive
integer, excluding terminal gaps).
.TP
\f[V]opens\f[R]
Number of gap-opening columns in the alignment (zero or positive
integer, excluding terminal gaps).
.TP
\f[V]exts\f[R]
Number of gap-extension columns in the alignment (zero or positive
integer).
.TP
\f[V]pairs\f[R]
Number of columns containing only nucleotides (alignment length minus
gap-containing columns; zero or positive integer).
.TP
\f[V]pv\f[R]
Number of positive columns.
Equivalent to the number of matches for nucleotide sequences.
.TP
\f[V]pctgaps\f[R]
Number of gap-containing columns expressed as a percentage of the
alignment length (real value from 0.0 to 100.0).
.TP
\f[V]pctpv\f[R]
Percentage of positive columns.
Equivalent to the percentage of matches for nucleotide sequences (real
value from 0.0 to 100.0).
.SS Identity percentages
.TP
\f[V]id\f[R]
Percentage of identity computed according to the definition selected by
\f[V]--iddef\f[R] (default: \f[V]id2\f[R]; real value from 0.0 to
100.0).
.TP
\f[V]id0\f[R]
CD-HIT definition: 100 * (matching columns) / (shortest sequence
length).
.TP
\f[V]id1\f[R]
Edit distance: 100 * (matching columns) / (alignment length).
.TP
\f[V]id2\f[R]
Edit distance excluding terminal gaps: 100 * (matching columns) /
(alignment length - terminal gaps).
Default definition for \f[V]--id\f[R].
.TP
\f[V]id3\f[R]
Marine Biological Lab definition, counting each gap opening (internal or
terminal) as a single mismatch, whether or not the gap was extended: 100
* (1.0 - [(mismatches + gap openings) / (longest sequence length)]).
.TP
\f[V]id4\f[R]
BLAST definition, equivalent to \f[V]id1\f[R] for global pairwise
alignments.
Always equal to \f[V]id1\f[R].
.SS Coverage
.TP
\f[V]qcov\f[R]
Fraction of the query sequence aligned with the target (real value from
0.0 to 100.0).
Computed as 100 * (matches + mismatches) / (query sequence length).
Gap-only columns are not counted.
.TP
\f[V]tcov\f[R]
Fraction of the target sequence aligned with the query (real value from
0.0 to 100.0).
Computed as 100 * (matches + mismatches) / (target sequence length).
Gap-only columns are not counted.
.SS Score
.TP
\f[V]raw\f[R]
Raw alignment score (negative, zero, or positive integer).
The score is the sum of match rewards minus mismatch penalties, gap
opening penalties, and gap extension penalties, using the parameters set
by \f[V]--match\f[R], \f[V]--mismatch\f[R], \f[V]--gapopen\f[R], and
\f[V]--gapext\f[R].
.TP
\f[V]bits\f[R]
Bit score.
Not computed for nucleotide alignments.
Always 0.
.TP
\f[V]evalue\f[R]
E-value.
Not computed for nucleotide alignments.
Always -1.
.SS Strand
.TP
\f[V]qstrand\f[R]
Query strand orientation (\f[V]+\f[R] or \f[V]-\f[R] for nucleotide
sequences).
Empty if there is no alignment.
.TP
\f[V]tstrand\f[R]
Target strand orientation.
Always \f[V]+\f[R]: when a query matches a target on the reverse strand,
\f[V]tstrand\f[R] is \f[V]+\f[R] and \f[V]qstrand\f[R] is \f[V]-\f[R].
Empty if there is no alignment.
.SS Unused fields
.TP
\f[V]qframe\f[R]
Query reading frame (-3 to +3).
Only meaningful for coding sequences; not computed by vsearch.
Always \f[V]+0\f[R].
.TP
\f[V]tframe\f[R]
Target reading frame (-3 to +3).
Only meaningful for coding sequences; not computed by vsearch.
Always \f[V]+0\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Output query label, target label, identity, alignment length, and number
of mismatches:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
vsearch \[rs]
    --usearch_global queries.fasta \[rs]
    --db db.fasta \[rs]
    --id 0.97 \[rs]
    --userout results.tsv \[rs]
    --userfields query+target+id+alnlen+mism
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Output all five identity definitions side by side for comparison:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
vsearch \[rs]
    --usearch_global queries.fasta \[rs]
    --db db.fasta \[rs]
    --id 0.0 \[rs]
    --userout identity_comparison.tsv \[rs]
    --userfields query+target+id0+id1+id2+id3+id4
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Output query coverage and alignment span excluding terminal gaps:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
vsearch \[rs]
    --usearch_global queries.fasta \[rs]
    --db db.fasta \[rs]
    --id 0.8 \[rs]
    --userout coverage.tsv \[rs]
    --userfields query+target+qcov+tcov+qilo+qihi+tilo+tihi
\f[R]
.fi
